---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import banner from "../../assets/work/articles/twilight-banner.jpg";

const tags = ["Twilight", "Cycling", "Athens", "Event Coverage"];
---

<Base
  title="Former racer returns to Twilight Criterium | Grace Joy Park"
  description="Grace Joy Park's vignette on a former Twilight racer scouting the downtown Athens course before the 46th Athens Orthopedic Clinic Twilight Criterium."
>
  <p class="back"><a href="/work">&larr; Back to Work</a></p>

  <article class="post">
    <h1>Former racer returns to Athens Orthopedic Clinic Twilight Criterium as vendors prepare for race weekend</h1>
    <p class="meta muted">Reporting I, Grady College &middot; April 17, 2026 &middot; By Grace Park</p>

    <ul class="tags">
      {tags.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
    </ul>

    <figure class="hero">
      <Image
        src={banner}
        alt="Twilight Criterium banner over the Silver Dollar Bar"
        widths={[600, 900, 1200, 1600]}
        sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 900px"
        format="webp"
      />
      <figcaption>
        A banner for the 46th Athens Orthopedic Clinic Twilight Criterium hangs above the
        Silver Dollar Bar on Friday, April 17, 2026, ahead of the race weekend in downtown
        Athens. (Photo/Grace Park)
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        Former Twilight racer Luke Harris rode through downtown Athens on Friday afternoon
        with the UGA Cycling group, scouting the course a day before the 46th Athens
        Orthopedic Clinic Twilight Criterium begins its pro races.
      </p>
      <p>
        &ldquo;We are here doing a little fun ride and checking all the stuff out today,&rdquo;
        Harris said. Harris came with the UGA Cycling group and previously competed at
        Twilight with Kingdom, a cycling team. He expressed excitement and anticipation
        for the upcoming men and women pro races.
      </p>
      <p>
        Around him, the 46th Athens Orthopedic Clinic Twilight Criterium was still
        preparing for its first full night. Food court vendors were setting up to serve
        the Athens community. Musicians ran through sound checks ahead of the ALL THINGS
        ATHENS concert on the Washington Street stage. Other cyclists rode through the
        streets, some stopping to do tricks or browse the vendor tents.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="story-links">
      <p>
        <a href="https://www.24liveblog.com/live/GbGUz?n=4090653707984968993" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          View the live coverage on Grady NewsSource &rarr;
        </a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/work/twilight-criterium.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Read the full story (PDF) &rarr;
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="reel-section">
      <h2>Reel</h2>
      <p class="reel-intro muted">
        My field reel from Twilight weekend, posted to Instagram and tagged @ugagrady.
      </p>
      <div class="reel-wrap">
        <blockquote
          class="instagram-media"
          data-instgrm-permalink="https://www.instagram.com/p/DXcYo5viZgU/"
          data-instgrm-version="14"
        ></blockquote>
      </div>
      <script async src="https://www.instagram.com/embed.js"></script>
    </section>

    <section class="why-section">
      <h2>Why I Wrote The Story</h2>
      <p>
        Twilight was a field assignment, but it was a real one. Half of downtown shuts
        down the weekend it runs and people were looking for any kind of preview.
        Walking up to a stranger in cycling gear and asking him questions on camera
        was the part I had been avoiding all semester, and once I did it I realized
        the rest of the reporting was just describing what was already happening
        around me. The hardest part was deciding what to leave out. There was a band
        soundchecking, food court tents going up and cyclists tricking through the
        closed streets, and only one of those details belonged in the lede.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .back { margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }

  .post h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .tags {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .tags li {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .hero {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .hero :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .hero figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .prose p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .prose .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .full-link {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .story-links {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .story-links p {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .story-links p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .reel-section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .reel-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .reel-intro {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .reel-wrap {
    max-width: 540px;
  }

  .reel-wrap :global(.instagram-media) {
    min-width: 0 !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  .why-section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .why-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .why-section p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
